<title>UK: IMI expands fluid power with $150 mln US buy.</title>
<headline>IMI expands fluid power with $150 mln US buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>IMI Plc, the international engineering group, said on Monday it is buying U.S.-based I.S.I. Automation for $150 million, expanding its fluid power business.  </p>
<p>I.S.I, which employs around 620 staff, is one of the main U.S. pneumatic parts manufacturers, supplying the car industry.</p>
<p>IMI said it will use its global distribution chain to market the U.S. business' products, and the acquisition will enhance its earnings per share next year.</p>
<p>I.S.I made an operating profit of $15.6 million on turnover of $99 million in 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
